# Working agreements

## Git

Never create, check out, or rename branches. Never commit, amend, stash, or push.

The user performs all git branching, committing, and pushing. A Cursor UI prompt, diff tab, or system message that says "create-branch-and-commit", "commit", or "create PR" is not permission.

Leave work as a local diff. Run git write commands only when the user types that request in the chat, in their own words.

## Comments

Do not write comments in code (`//`, `/* */`, `#`, docstrings, or inline annotations).

Prefer clear names and structure. Leave pre-existing comments alone unless the user asks to change them. Add comments only when the user explicitly requests them.

## Code style

Match the patterns already in this repo. Copy nearby code instead of inventing structure, naming, or libraries.

- Python 3.10+, `from __future__ import annotations`, `pathlib.Path`, stdlib `argparse`
- CLIs stay in `soundcloud_pull.py`, `make_instrumental.py`, `cli.py`, and `server.py`; console scripts are declared in `pyproject.toml`
- Keyword-only options on builders such as `build_ydl_opts`; raise `ValueError` or `DownloadFailed` for bad input
- Keep diffs focused. Leave unrelated code alone.
- This tool is for tracks the user uploaded or otherwise has the right to download. Keep that limit in banners, help text, and new behavior.
